      m_Calls: []
  m_text: 'Snow settles on what faces up. Shader Surface/Snow-Top measures, for every pixel, how much the surface faces up in the world, and mixes in the snow (colour, smoothness, a flatter normal) above a threshold set by Snow Amount.


    <b>Predict:</b> You turn the block on the left 90 degrees around Z, onto its side. Where is the snow afterwards?


    <b>Try:</b> Rotate the blocks and the bench in the Scene view. Change Snow Amount (M_Surf_Snow-Concrete). Set Snow Color to a light brown-grey: the same layer becomes dust.'
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 2f7116f10747a67409388e93052ae222, type: 2}
