  m_OnCullStateChanged:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
  m_text: 'A wet surface is darker (water fills the pores) and smoother (a film of water). Shader Surface/Wet-Puddles has a slider for each: Wet Darkening and Wet Smoothness. A is dry; B is only darker; C is only smoother; D is both. The light box behind them gives them something to reflect.


    <b>Predict:</b> Which of B, C and D looks wet?


    <b>Try:</b> Select C''s material (M_Surf_Wet-C-Smoother) and raise Wet Darkening. On B''s material (M_Surf_Wet-B-Darker), raise Wet Smoothness. Orbit low over the slabs.


    <size=85%><color=#A8A8A8>Reference: Material chart: wet asphalt</color></size>'
